            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Late spring through early fall in most regions, on a day when air and pavement are at least 50°F and stay there for 24 hours, with no rain forecast. In hot southern climates, spring and fall are often easier than midsummer. Avoid late-season jobs where nights drop into the 40s, since the coat may not cure fully."
