        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most asphalt driveways need sealer every two to three years, concrete driveways somewhere between every two and every ten years depending on the product, and pavers every three to five. The water test is the deciding check: if water beads, wait; if it soaks in, it is time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Put your effort where it pays off most. Fill cracks every year they appear, keep the surface clean, and seal when the surface asks for it rather than when a flyer does. That routine costs less than annual coating and does more to keep the driveway sound for decades.
          </p>
